# Berkeley in-person outreach calendar

Standing venues, recurring series with their fixed cadence, and the hard term dates that bound when
anyone is on campus. Specific one-off talk dates aren't all published yet; where a series hasn't posted
its next speaker, the live feed to watch is listed. Updated 2026-11-19.

## The window: act before 4 December 2026

The in-person window closes fast. UC Berkeley Fall 2026:
- **Thanksgiving:** Nov 25 non-instructional, Nov 26–27 holiday — campus dead that week.
- **Formal classes end:** Friday, December 4, 2026.
- **Reading/Review week:** Dec 7–11 (seminars mostly stop; students in exam mode).
- **Last day of instruction:** Friday, December 11. **Finals:** Dec 14–18.
- **Spring instruction begins:** Tuesday, January 19, 2027.

So the live seminar/catch-people-in-the-hall window is now through **Dec 4**, minus Thanksgiving week —
effectively **this week (Nov 19–21) and Nov 30–Dec 4**. After Dec 4 the campus empties until Jan 19, 2027.
The Simons atrium and labs stay partly active through mid-December, but the seminar series stop.

## The subject-matched one: foundations of computing

**Simons Institute for the Theory of Computing** — Calvin Lab, on the UC Berkeley campus (northeast side,
near Hearst Mining Circle; not Berkeley Way West — that was an error in the first version). Open-door by
design: atrium, coffee, visiting fellows, public talks you can sit in on with no invitation. The crowd
who would actually read a univalent-foundations argument, reachable informally with no gate. Fall 2026
programs (Pseudorandomness & High-Dimensional Expansion; Spectral Theory Beyond Graphs) run through the
term, so fellows are in-building on weekdays into mid-December.
- Live calendar for dated talks: https://simons.berkeley.edu/calendar
- Walk-in: any weekday, the atrium. Highest-yield before Dec 4.

## The AI hub: Sutardja Dai Hall, 2594 Hearst Ave

**CITRIS Research Exchange** — the one with a fixed, reliable cadence: **Wednesdays, 12:00–1:00 pm Pacific,
Banatao Auditorium (310 Sutardja Dai Hall), free and open to the public.** Has hosted Stuart Russell and
Anca Dragan in past terms. Remaining Wednesdays this term: **Nov 25** (Thanksgiving week — likely no talk)
and **Dec 2** (probable last of the term). People stand around before and after; that's the conversation
window.
- Schedule / speakers: https://citris-uc.org/citris-research-exchange

**CHAI AI Risk Speaker Series** — talks on AI risk from academia, industry and civil society, in Sutardja
Dai Hall. No specific talk is posted right now ("next talks are being scheduled"; most recent was Emma
Pierson, Nov 17). Watch the live feed and ask the organizer directly:
- Google Calendar + mailing list: https://ai-risk.berkeley.edu
- Organizer: Will Fithian, wfithian@berkeley.edu
- Reaches: Stuart Russell, Anca Dragan (CHAI), Andrew Critch.

**CLIMB / Voleon Seminar** — 310 Sutardja Dai Hall, ML/decision-theory. Ariel Procaccia (the social-choice
theorist whose impossibility results are load-bearing in the field email) spoke here Oct 2025. No upcoming
date posted; check https://climb.berkeley.edu/seminars.

**Soda Hall** — next door, EECS and the BAIR lab. Morning-entrance tactic; same people.

## The science-of-happiness node: Berkeley Way West, 2121 Berkeley Way

**Dacher Keltner's Social Interaction Lab** and the **Greater Good Science Center**, both of which he
directs, plus the Psychology department offices. He is a former teacher of yours — email first, then visit,
not a cold hallway catch. Front desk knows his schedule; verify current-term teaching at
https://classes.berkeley.edu before relying on a room/time. Same Dec 4 window applies.

## Annual, not walk-in

**CHAI Annual Workshop** — Asilomar (Pacific Grove), early June, registration. The one time most of the
human-compatible-AI community is in one room. Target for June 2027. https://humancompatible.ai

